(window.DETAIL_C = window.DETAIL_C || {})["mth-12-14"] = {"mth-12-14-m01":{"idea":"A random variable turns each outcome into a number.","steps":["Take an experiment, for example tossing three coins.","Count the heads: the count is 0, 1, 2 or 3 depending on the outcome.","That rule, which gives one real number per outcome, is a random variable."],"others":"A number that never changes is a constant. Saying its values cannot be listed describes only continuous ones. The probability of an event is a different thing.","trap":"It is a function, not a probability.","answer":"a function that gives a real number for each outcome of an experiment"},"mth-12-14-m02":{"idea":"Discrete means the values are found by counting.","steps":["Count the heads in 5 tosses: the value is 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5.","These are separate whole numbers, so the variable is discrete.","Height, weight and time are measured and can take any value in an interval."],"others":"Height, weight and race time are measured, so they are continuous.","trap":"Counting gives discrete, measuring gives continuous.","answer":"the number of heads in 5 tosses of a coin"},"mth-12-14-m03":{"idea":"Continuous means measured, with any value in an interval.","steps":["The life of a bulb can be any positive real number.","It is measured in time, not counted.","So it is continuous. The other three are counts."],"others":"Students in a class, bulbs failing in a month and sixes in 10 throws are all counts.","trap":"Time is continuous.","answer":"the time a bulb works before it fails"},"mth-12-14-m04":{"idea":"A probability is never negative and all probabilities add to 1.","steps":["Each probability pᵢ is zero or positive.","One of the values must occur, so the total is 1.","These are the two conditions."],"others":"A total of 0 is impossible. Negative probabilities do not exist. Each pᵢ cannot be at least 1 unless there is only one value.","trap":"Total must be exactly 1.","answer":"each pᵢ ≥ 0, and p₁ + p₂ + … + pₙ = 1"},"mth-12-14-m05":{"idea":"The probabilities must add up to 1.","steps":["The probabilities are k, 2k, 3k, 4k and 5k.","Their sum is 15k.","15k = 1, so k = 1/15."],"others":"1/10 would need a sum of 10k. 1/20 and 1/5 come from wrong sums.","trap":"Add 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15.","answer":"1/15"},"mth-12-14-m06":{"idea":"Each value is weighted by its probability.","steps":["Multiply each value xᵢ by its probability pᵢ.","Add all of these products.","E(X) = Σ xᵢ pᵢ."],"others":"Squares times probabilities give E(X²). The sum of probabilities is 1. The plain average works only if all probabilities are equal.","trap":"Weight, then add.","answer":"E(X) = Σ xᵢ pᵢ, the sum of each value times its probability"},"mth-12-14-m07":{"idea":"Variance is the mean of the squares minus the square of the mean.","steps":["Var(X) = Σ(xᵢ − μ)²pᵢ.","Expanding gives Σxᵢ²pᵢ − μ².","So Var(X) = E(X²) − [E(X)]²."],"others":"Adding the squared mean gives a bigger number. Reversing the order gives a negative number. E(X²) − E(X) does not square the mean.","trap":"Square the mean after finding it.","answer":"Var(X) = E(X²) − [E(X)]²"},"mth-12-14-m08":{"idea":"Standard deviation brings the spread back to the units of X.","steps":["Variance is in squared units.","Take the positive square root.","That gives the standard deviation."],"others":"It is not the mean. It is not the reciprocal of the variance. It is not the variance squared.","trap":"Root, not square.","answer":"the positive square root of Var(X)"},"mth-12-14-m09":{"idea":"F collects probability, so it only grows.","steps":["F(x) = P(X ≤ x).","As x grows, more values are included, so F cannot fall.","For very large x all values are included, so F tends to 1."],"others":"A limit of 0 at large x is wrong. A probability total cannot be negative. F does not decrease.","trap":"F rises from 0 to 1.","answer":"it never decreases, and it tends to 1 for large x"},"mth-12-14-m10":{"idea":"A single point has no width, so no area.","steps":["For a continuous variable, probability is the area under the density curve.","A single point has zero width.","So the area, and the probability, is zero."],"others":"The height of the density is not a probability. The cumulative value at a point is P(X ≤ a). A probability of one is for the whole range.","trap":"Probability only for intervals.","answer":"zero, as probability is found from the area under the density curve"},"mth-12-14-m11":{"idea":"A density must be non-negative with total area 1.","steps":["The height f(x) cannot be negative.","The total area under the curve is the total probability, which is 1.","Both conditions are needed."],"others":"A height of at most 1 is not required. A density need not be a whole number. A bound of 1 on the height says nothing about the area.","trap":"The area is 1, the height can be more.","answer":"f(x) ≥ 0 for all x, and the total area under it is 1"},"mth-12-14-m12":{"idea":"Check the area, not the height.","steps":["The base is 0.5 and the height is 2.","The area is 2 × 0.5 = 1.","So it is a valid density, even though the height is above 1."],"others":"A height above 1 is allowed. Being zero everywhere is not required. The area here is 1, not 2.","trap":"Height is a density per unit of x.","answer":"a valid density function, since the area is 2 × 0.5 = 1"},"mth-12-14-m13":{"idea":"Probability over an interval is the area under the density.","steps":["Take the area under the curve from a to b.","In symbols, that is the integral of f(x) from a to b.","This is the probability of X falling in that interval."],"others":"The product of one height and the width treats the curve as flat. A sum of end heights has no meaning. A difference of end heights is a change in height, not an area.","trap":"Area, not height.","answer":"the integral of f(x) from a to b"},"mth-12-14-m14":{"idea":"F is the running area, and f is the slope of F.","steps":["F(x) is the area under f from the start a up to x.","By the fundamental theorem of calculus, the derivative of that area is f(x).","So F(x) is the integral of f, and f(x) = F′(x)."],"others":"f is not the integral of F. F and f are not equal. F is not the derivative of f.","trap":"Integrate f to get F, differentiate F to get f.","answer":"F(x) is the integral of f from a to x, and f(x) = F′(x)"},"mth-12-14-m15":{"idea":"Variance scales with the square of the multiplier and ignores shifts.","steps":["Var(aX + b) = a² Var(X).","Here the multiplier is 3 and the shift is 2.","Var(3X + 2) = 9 × 2 = 18."],"others":"6 multiplies by 3 only. 20 adds the shift. 8 uses 2 × 2 + 4.","trap":"Square the multiplier, ignore the shift.","answer":"18"},"mth-12-14-m16":{"idea":"Find the smallest and largest sums.","steps":["The smallest sum is 1 + 1 = 2.","The largest sum is 6 + 6 = 12.","Every whole number from 2 to 12 is possible, which gives 11 values."],"others":"36 is the number of outcomes, not of values. 1 to 12 includes 1, which is impossible. 6 is the number of faces.","trap":"Values, not outcomes.","answer":"11, the whole numbers from 2 to 12"},"mth-12-14-m17":{"idea":"The probabilities add up to 1.","steps":["0.2 + p + 0.5 = 1.","p = 1 − 0.7.","p = 0.3."],"others":"0.5 and 0.7 come from wrong subtraction. 0.1 uses a wrong total.","trap":"Find the unknown first.","answer":"0.3"},"mth-12-14-m18":{"idea":"Average the six faces.","steps":["E(X) = (1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6)/6.","The sum is 21.","21/6 = 3.5."],"others":"21 is the sum, not the mean. 3.0 and 4.0 are not the average of the faces.","trap":"Divide by 6.","answer":"3.5"},"mth-12-14-m19":{"idea":"A variance cannot be negative.","steps":["Var(X) = Σ(xᵢ − μ)²pᵢ.","Each term is a square times a probability, so it is zero or positive.","A negative answer means an error, often E(X²) and [E(X)]² taken in the wrong order."],"others":"A variance is never negative. It also need not be more than 1. A mean larger than E(X²) cannot happen.","trap":"Variance is zero or more.","answer":"wrong, as a variance is a sum of squares times probabilities, and it cannot be negative"},"mth-12-14-m20":{"idea":"F adds probability in lumps at each value.","steps":["F(x) = Σ pᵢ over all xᵢ ≤ x.","It stays flat between the values of X.","It jumps up by pᵢ at each xᵢ, so it is a step function."],"others":"F is not constant. It is not a straight line of slope 1. It is not smooth, because it jumps.","trap":"Discrete means steps.","answer":"a step function, that jumps by pᵢ at each value xᵢ"},"mth-12-14-m21":{"idea":"Variance is not negative.","steps":["Var(X) = E(X²) − [E(X)]².","Variance is zero or more.","So E(X²) ≥ [E(X)]², with equality only if X is constant."],"others":"E(X²) = 2E(X) is false in general. E(X²) ≤ [E(X)]² would give a negative variance. Equality for every variable is false.","trap":"Mean of squares at least square of mean.","answer":"E(X²) ≥ [E(X)]², since the variance is not negative"},"mth-12-14-m22":{"idea":"Check the total area.","steps":["The integral of x from 0 to 1 is 1/2.","The area must be 1, so it fails.","Doubling gives f(x) = 2x, which has area 1."],"others":"Being a straight line is not a problem. Being zero outside the interval is normal. The function is not negative on the interval.","trap":"Area must be exactly 1.","answer":"the area under it is 1/2, not 1"},"mth-12-14-n01":{"idea":"The probabilities must add up to 1.","steps":["The probabilities are k, 2k, 3k, 4k and 5k.","They add up to 15k = 1.","So k = 1/15 = 0.0667."],"trap":"Sum 1 to 5 is 15.","answer":"0.0667"},"mth-12-14-n02":{"idea":"E(X) is the sum of value times probability.","steps":["E(X) = 1(0.1) + 2(0.2) + 3(0.3) + 4(0.4).","= 0.1 + 0.4 + 0.9 + 1.6.","E(X) = 3.0."],"trap":"Multiply each value by its own probability.","answer":"3"},"mth-12-14-n03":{"idea":"Use Var(X) = E(X²) − [E(X)]².","steps":["E(X²) = 1(0.1) + 4(0.2) + 9(0.3) + 16(0.4) = 10.","[E(X)]² = 3² = 9.","Var(X) = 10 − 9 = 1.00."],"trap":"Square the values, then weight.","answer":"1"},"mth-12-14-n04":{"idea":"The mean of a sum is the sum of the means.","steps":["For one die, E = 3.5.","For two dice, E(sum) = 3.5 + 3.5.","E(sum) = 7."],"trap":"Add the means.","answer":"7"},"mth-12-14-n05":{"idea":"Find the distribution of heads in 3 tosses, then the variance.","steps":["P(X = 0, 1, 2, 3) = 1/8, 3/8, 3/8, 1/8, so E(X) = 1.5.","E(X²) = 3/8 + 12/8 + 9/8 = 3.","Var(X) = 3 − 2.25 = 0.75."],"trap":"Subtract the square of the mean.","answer":"0.75"},"mth-12-14-n06":{"idea":"The total area must be 1.","steps":["The integral of kx² from 0 to 3 is k × 27/3 = 9k.","So 9k = 1.","Hence k = 1/9 = 0.1111."],"trap":"Integral of x² on [0, 3] is 9.","answer":"0.1111"},"mth-12-14-n07":{"idea":"Integrate the density over the interval.","steps":["P = the integral of x²/9 from 1 to 2.","= [x³/27] from 1 to 2 = (8 − 1)/27.","= 7/27 = 0.2593."],"trap":"Antiderivative of x²/9 is x³/27.","answer":"0.2593"},"mth-12-14-n08":{"idea":"E(X) is the integral of x times the density.","steps":["E(X) = the integral of x × 2x dx from 0 to 1.","= the integral of 2x² dx = [2x³/3] from 0 to 1.","= 2/3 = 0.6667."],"trap":"Multiply the density by x first.","answer":"0.6667"},"mth-12-14-n09":{"idea":"Set the cumulative function equal to 1/2.","steps":["F(x) = the integral of 2t dt from 0 to x = x².","Set x² = 1/2.","m = 1/√2 = 0.7071."],"trap":"Median splits the area into halves.","answer":"0.7071"},"mth-12-14-n10":{"idea":"Expected winnings minus the price.","steps":["E(winnings) = 30 × 1/6 + 10 × 1/6 + 0 × 4/6 = 40/6 = 6.67.","Net gain = 6.67 − 10.","= −3.33, so on average a player loses ₹3.33 per game."],"trap":"A negative answer is a loss.","answer":"-3.33"}};
